            "review_title": "Review at The River Cafe",
            "review_text": "frank v\nHo Chi Minh City, Vietnam95 contributions\n0\nDisappointing\nFeb 2017 • Family\nI took my family there on a week end lunch. The truth is I wasn't expecting much given the modest gate, and the place looked as expected: mostly temporary DIY construction & furniture.\nThe prices are average, again given the basic looks I was expecting lower prices. The service was partly very good as one waiter could speak fluent English and partly very poor because the other waiter or helper was hopeless, and had unkept nails which always bothers me in a restaurant.\nThe food was the same the tofu was very good, the morning glory and fried rice were average and the beef luc lac was inedible.\nThe beef on the menu is supposed to be Aussie beef, but the only thing Aussie was how tough it was. It was so bad we sent it back, but it came back just the same.\nWe were sitting by the water and the amount of rubbish floating around and the foul odors did not help... but you can choose to sit further from the water to avoid this.\nIt has some kind of a DIY built play caban for kids, but it does not look very safe.\nI think they were inspired by snap cafe, but it does not measure up in any way, except for the tofu!\nThe riverside location could do so much better!\nI won't be going back...\nRead more\nWritten February 15, 2017",
